{"name":"Dover Grey","hex":"#848585","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dover","blocks":[{"text":"Dover is a town, major ferry port and civil parish in Kent, England. It faces France across the Strait of Dover, the narrowest part of the English Channel at 33 kilometres (21 mi) from Cap Gris-Nez in France. It lies southeast of Canterbury and east of Maidstone. The town is the administrative centre of the Dover District and home of the Port of Dover. In 2024 it had an estimated population of 44,209."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Dover_from_the_top_of_Dover_Castle_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4061940.jpg/330px-Dover_from_the_top_of_Dover_Castle_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4061940.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dover"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Dover_Town_Hall_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2321356.jpg/500px-Dover_Town_Hall_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2321356.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Dover_Town_Hal